{"id": "9th-u1-q033", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "assertion_reason", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-solvalam-semmozhi", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கூற்று (A): ஒரே பொருளைக் குறிக்கப் பல சொற்கள் அமைந்த சொல்வளமும் சொல்லாட்சியும் நிரம்பிய பெருமொழி தமிழாகும்.\nகாரணம் (R): ஒரு தாவரத்தின் இலை நிலைகளை மட்டும் குறிக்க இலை, தாள், தோகை, ஓலை, சண்டு, சருகு எனப் பல நுட்பமான சொற்களைக் கொண்டுள்ள ஒரே மொழி தமிழ்.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் சரி; காரணம் கூற்றை விளக்குகிறது", "B": "கூற்று (A) சரி, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) தவறு", "C": "கூற்று (A) தவறு, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) சரி", "D": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் தவறு"}, "explanation": "தமிழின் நிகரற்ற சொல்வளத்திற்குத் தாவர உறுப்புகளின் பெயர்களே அசைக்க முடியாத சான்றாகும். கூற்று மற்றும் காரணம் இரண்டும் முற்றிலும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assertion (A): Tamil is exceptionally renowned for its rich semantic vocabulary, using distinct words to describe micro-variations of a single entity.\nReason (R): For instance, Tamil possesses specialized vocabulary for different stages of plant leaves (Ilai, Thaal, Thogai, Olai, Sandu, Sarugu).", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are correct, and (R) correctly explains (A)", "B": "(A) is correct, but (R) is false", "C": "(A) is false, but (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false"}, "explanation": "Both (A) and (R) are factually true and illustrate the exquisite botanical and lexical precision of Tamil."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 9, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 9", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tamil_richness", "vocabulary_precision", "assertion_reason"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q045", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-sol-thotram", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'தமிழ்' என்னும் சொல்லிலிருந்தே 'திராவிடம்' என்னும் சொல் பிறந்தது என்று மொழியியல் அடிப்படையில் விளக்கிய பாதிரியார் யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஹீராஸ் பாதிரியார்", "B": "கால்டுவெல் பாதிரியார்", "C": "போப் பாதிரியார்", "D": "பெஸ்கி பாதிரியார்"}, "explanation": "ஹீராஸ் பாதிரியார் தமிழ் என்னும் சொல்லிலிருந்து 'திராவிடம்' உருவான ஒலி மாற்றத்தை (தமிழ் → தமழா → த்ரமில → த்ரமிட → த்ராவிட → திராவிடம்) விளக்கினார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which historian-priest demonstrated phonologically that the word 'Dravida' was derived directly from the word 'Tamil'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Father Heras", "B": "Bishop Caldwell", "C": "Rev. G.U. Pope", "D": "Father Beschi"}, "explanation": "Father Henry Heras demonstrated the historical linguistic trajectory leading from 'Tamil' to 'Dravidam'."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 5, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 5", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["heras", "etymology", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q046", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-podhukkoorugal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் பொதுக்கூறுகள் குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. திராவிட மொழிகளில் பெரும்பாலானவை ஒட்டுநிலை (Agglutinative) மொழிகளாக விளங்குகின்றன.\n2. சொற்களின் வேர்ச்சொல்லோடு விகுதிகள் ஒன்றன் பின் ஒன்றாக இணைந்து புதிய பொருளைத் தருகின்றன.\n3. வடமொழியைப் போலன்றித் திராவிட மொழிகளில் சொற்களின் வேர் வடிவம் பெரும்பாலும் மாறாமல் மூலப் பொருளைக் காக்கிறது.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "அனைத்தும் சரி", "C": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி"}, "explanation": "திராவிட மொழிகள் ஒட்டுநிலை மொழிகள் (Agglutinative languages). வேர்ச்சொல்லுடன் விகுதிகள் சேரும் போது மூலப்பொருள் கெடாமல் நிற்கும். எனவே அனைத்துக் கூற்றுகளும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Analyze the common morphological characteristics of Dravidian languages:\n1. Most Dravidian languages are agglutinative in their morphological structure.\n2. Affixes and suffixes are suffixed sequentially to root bases to yield inflected meanings.\n3. Unlike inflected Indo-European tongues, the semantic integrity of the Dravidian root remains identifiable.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct", "C": "2 and 3 only are correct", "D": "1 and 3 only are correct"}, "explanation": "Agglutination and preserved root integrity are classic hallmarks of the Dravidian linguistic family."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 9, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 9", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["agglutination", "morphology", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q053", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-moolachol-porutham", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் சொல் ஒற்றுமை குறித்த பின்வரும் இணைகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. மரம் - தமிழ் மற்றும் மலையாளத்தில் ஒரே வடிவைக் கொண்டுள்ளது.\n2. கண் - தமிழ், மலையாளம், கன்னடம், தெலுங்கு, குடகு ஆகிய அனைத்திலும் 'கண்/கண்ணு' என்றே வேர்ச்சொல் அமைகிறது.\n3. மூன்று - துளு மொழியில் 'மூறு' என வழங்குகிறது.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியான இணைகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "துளு மொழியில் 'மூன்று' என்பது 'மூஜி' என வழங்குகிறது ('மூறு' என்பது கன்னடத்தில் வழங்குகிறது). எனவே கூற்று 3 தவறு; 1 மற்றும் 2 சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statements regarding lexical cognates across Dravidian languages:\n1. 'Maram' shares an identical phonetic shape in both Tamil and Malayalam.\n2. The root for eye ('Kan/Kannu') is shared identically across Tamil, Malayalam, Kannada, Telugu, and Kodagu.\n3. The numeral 'Three' is pronounced as 'Mooru' in Tulu.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "2 and 3 only are correct", "C": "1 and 3 only are correct", "D": "All are correct"}, "explanation": "In Tulu, three is 'Mooji' ('Mooru' is in Kannada). Statements 1 and 2 are correct."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["lexical_cognates", "tulu_numerals", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q054", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-oppilakkana-thanthai", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணத் தந்தை' என்று தமிழ்நாடு முழுமையாலும் போற்றப்படும் அறிஞர் யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஜி.யு. போப்", "B": "ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல்", "C": "பிரான்சிஸ் எல்லிஸ்", "D": "வீரமாமுனிவர்"}, "explanation": "1856-இல் வெளியான 'திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணம்' நூலின் மூலம் திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பத்தின் தனித்தன்மையை உலகுக்கு நிலைநாட்டிய ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல் 'திராவிட ஒப்பிலக்கணத் தந்தை' எனப் போற்றப்படுகிறார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Who is widely honored as the 'Father of Comparative Dravidian Linguistics'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Rev. G.U. Pope", "B": "Dr. Robert Caldwell", "C": "Francis Whyte Ellis", "D": "Constanzo Beschi"}, "explanation": "Dr. Robert Caldwell is universally celebrated as the Father of Comparative Dravidian Linguistics for his monumental 1856 treatise."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "