{"id": "10th-u6-q139", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "single_choice", "level": "standard", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "10", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_6", "lesson_id": "agapporul_ilakkanam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "kaikkilai_perunthinai", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "அகத்திணையில் \"ஒருதலைக் காமம்\" மற்றும் \"பொருந்தாக் காமம்\" முறையே எவ்வாறு அழைக்கப்படுகின்றன?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "முல்லை, மருதம்", "B": "குறிஞ்சி, பாலை", "C": "கைக்கிளை (ஒருதலைக் காமம்) மற்றும் பெருந்திணை (பொருந்தாக் காமம்)", "D": "நெய்தல், பாலை"}, "explanation": "ஒருவர் மட்டுமே விரும்பும் ஒருதலைக் காதல் \"கைக்கிளை\" எனப்படும்; வயது அல்லது நிலை பொருந்தாத முரண் காதல் \"பெருந்திணை\" எனப்படும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In classical Tamil poetics, what are unrequited one-sided love and mismatched/inappropriate love termed respectively?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Mullai and Marutham", "B": "Kurinji and Paalai", "C": "Kaikkilai (One-sided love) and Perunthinai (Mismatched love)", "D": "Neithal and Paalai"}, "explanation": "Kaikkilai represents unrequited love and Perunthinai denotes mismatched union."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "10", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025"