{"id": "11th_tamil_u1_q164", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "hard", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_1", "lesson_id": "grammar_first_last_letters", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "tholkappiyam_vs_nannool_gn", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தொல்காப்பியர் காலத்தில் ‘ஞ’ வரிசையில் ‘ஞ, ஞா, ஞெ’ ஆகிய மூன்று மட்டுமே முதலில் வந்தன; நன்னூலார் காலத்தில் இதனுடன் கூடுதலாக இணைந்த நான்காவது எழுத்து எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஞி", "B": "ஞு", "C": "ஞை", "D": "ஞொ (எ.கா: ஞொள்கிற்று)"}, "explanation": "தொல்காப்பியர் காலத்தில் ஞ, ஞா, ஞெ மட்டுமே மொழி முதலில் வந்தன; பிற்காலத்தில் நன்னூலார் காலத்தில் ‘ஞொ’ (ஞொள்கிற்று) என்னும் எழுத்தும் மொழி முதலில் வந்தது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "While Tholkappiyar permitted only Gna, Gnaa, and Gne initially, which fourth letter was added by Nannoolar reflecting linguistic evolution?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Gni", "B": "Gnu", "C": "Gnai", "D": "Gno (ஞொ as in Gnolgirru)"}, "explanation": "Nannool incorporated 'Gno' (ஞொ) into the initial Gna series."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 14, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference