{"id": "12th_tamil_u8_q1499", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_8", "lesson_id": "kuriyeedu_grammar", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "fox_cunning_symbol", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "பழமொழிகளிலும் கதைகளிலும் ‘நரி’ எத்தகைய மனிதப் பண்பிற்குக் குறியீடாக ஆளப்படுகிறது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "நேர்மை மற்றும் உண்மை", "B": "வீரம் மற்றும் தியாகம்", "C": "தந்திரம், வஞ்சகம் மற்றும் சுயநலச் சூழ்ச்சி", "D": "பயந்த சுபாவம்"}, "explanation": "நரி என்பது பிறரை ஏமாற்றித் தன் காரியத்தைச் சாதித்துக் கொள்ளும் வஞ்சகக் குணத்திற்கும் சூழ்ச்சிக்கும் குறியீடாகும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In fables and literary folklore, what human vice does the 'Fox' (Nari) conventionally represent?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Truth and integrity", "B": "Heroism and sacrifice", "C": "Cunning craftiness, deceitful trickery, and selfish opportunism", "D": "Timid fearfulness"}, "explanation": "The fox is universally employed as an allegory for cunning deceit and opportunism."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "12", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 210, "chapter": null, "section": nu